  <Docs>
    <summary>Represents one client invocation attempt performed by a <see cref="T:Microsoft.Extensions.AI.FailoverChatClient" />.</summary>
    <remarks>
      <para>
            A completed response has <see cref="P:Microsoft.Extensions.AI.FailoverChatClientAttempt.ResponseCompleted" /> set to <see langword="true" /> and
            <see cref="P:Microsoft.Extensions.AI.FailoverChatClientAttempt.Exception" /> set to <see langword="null" />.
            </para>
      <para>
            A failed invocation has <see cref="P:Microsoft.Extensions.AI.FailoverChatClientAttempt.ResponseCompleted" /> set to <see langword="false" /> and
            <see cref="P:Microsoft.Extensions.AI.FailoverChatClientAttempt.Exception" /> set to the observed exception. If a streaming caller stops enumerating before the
            response ends and disposal completes successfully, both <see cref="P:Microsoft.Extensions.AI.FailoverChatClientAttempt.ResponseCompleted" /> and
            <see cref="P:Microsoft.Extensions.AI.FailoverChatClientAttempt.Exception" /> are unset.
            </para>
      <para>
        <see cref="P:Microsoft.Extensions.AI.FailoverChatClientAttempt.OutputCommitted" /> is independent of the outcome and indicates whether any streaming update was
            exposed to the caller.
            </para>
    </remarks>
  </Docs>
